BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea4Tea - An All Trans and Nonbinary Comedy Mutual Aid Fundraiser!
DTSTART:20260416T200000
DTEND:20260416T200000
UID:97df638ef33607bc6506f752ed1afbb7@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:A night of EXCLUSIVELY trans and / or nonbinary comedians spil
 ling the tea for mutual aid directly supporting a family in Gaza We need t
 rans community and solidarity more than ever\, and that&#x27\;s what this 
 comedy show is all about! Come check out a line of EXCLUSIVELY trans and /
  or nonbinary comedians coming together in solidarity to make you belly la
 ugh. All proceeds from the show will go to the Sondos Project\, supporting
  a family of 13 living in Gaza 🏳️‍🌈🍉 Tea4Tea is all about hav
 ing a blast while gathering in community\, celebrating the amazing comedic
  talent in Toronto\, and getting some hard earned trans and queer joy! Thi
 s is an extra special fundraiser edition that is one small part of taking 
 care of each other in hard times. Doors 7 45 pm\, show 8 pm! Featuring: Wi
 lly Coombes (@willycoombes\, they/them\, certified They/Them Maheym) Orion
  Candelma (@xoxosatan\, she/they\, 0rionsbelt comedy and photography) Ada 
 Nicolle (@adanicklmao\, she/her\, Vibra Slap Comedy\, &quot\;Bags of Ice&q
 uot\; streaming everywhere) Anna Penner (@somequeerreads\, all pronouns\, 
 Heheheated Rivalry) Meg Mackay (@megmackaycomedy\, they/them\, Winnipeg Co
 medy Festival\, Crave\, Aborigional People&#x27\;s Television Network) Bee
  Bertrand (@beerbertrandcomedy\, he/him\, Just for Laughs\, Pride Radio) A
 va VAl (@avavalcomedy\, she/her\, Just for Laughs\, CBC\, CTV) Hosted and 
 produced by Anna Sebastien (@annasebastiencomedy\, they/them\, Just for La
 ughs Toronto\, Bad Gay Advice\, Fresh Hot Babes All Fem &amp\; Queer Comed
 y) Advanced tickets are $25 but all are welcome regardless of means - DM @
 annasebastiencomedy on Instagram for Pay What You Can tickets / community 
 pricing. All welcome including respectful allies who understand this is a 
 trans inclusive space where we don&#x27\;t assume anyone&#x27\;s pronouns\
 , gender\, or orientation 🥰 Again\, this show is all about community - 
 if you have any questions or are nervous about coming out\, please reach o
 ut to the producer at @annasebastiencomedy on Instagram or email at anna.s
 ebastien.comedy@gmail.com Hope to see you there! 😊 -- About the fundrai
 ser: From the Sondos Project website: Sondos and her family of 13 need our
  help for food and supplies. Sondos and her family are #388 on @palilibera
 tion&#x27\;s verified families list! You can follow Sonds here\, and the S
 ondos Project here. This campaign was chosen because it supports a family 
 directly and because the efforts of local drag artists to actually do some
 thing about the ongoing crisis in Gaza are inspiring AF! After compensatin
 g comedians (we love paying trans artists for their labour!)\, all proceed
 s will be donated. Receipts of the donation will be posted on the producer
 s Instagram for transperancy. Can&#x27\;t make the show but want to suppor
 t? Love that. Donate here. About the venue: The show takes place at Tallbo
 ys (838 Bloor W\, near Ossington subway station) The show takes place in t
 he theatre space in the downstairs area of Tallboys. Take a left when you 
 walk in and head downstairs! The venue unfortunately has a few barriers to
  access. There is a large step to enter the main bar area. The theatre spa
 ce and washrooms are located down a staircase\, with tight corners from th
 e bottom landing to the theatre. There is also a single step from the base
 ment hallway into the venue room. Once inside\, there is no grade change. 
 All communal washrooms in the venue are gender neutral. There is also an u
 nmarked\, single stall\, gender neutral washroom with a toilet. There is a
  full kitchen available until 10 pm\, and non-alcoholic and alcoholic beve
 rages available until close No purchase is required on top of your ticket 
 (but we love it when you support the venue if ya can!) ‍
LOCATION:Tallboys Craft Beer House\, 838 Bloor Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/tea4tea---an-all-trans-and-nonbinary-comed
 y-mutual-aid-fundraiser
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LE CABARET BLEU: Le Jardin des Papillons
DTSTART:20260416T200000
DTEND:20260416T200000
UID:2f0e4be644387ba055b32fe9c103f1c8@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:A VINTAGE CABARET SOIREE! Featuring our live jazz band and Tor
 onto&#x27\;s finest cabaret talent. 🎪 The Night Circus Toronto Presents
 : Le Cabaret Bleu – Le Jardin des Papillons 📅 April 16th 📍 The Pai
 nted Lady\, Toronto ⏰ 8:00 PM – Late ✨ Pre-show: 8:30 PM | Show Star
 t: 9 PM 🎟 Seating first come\, first serve! Tickets Advance Tickets: $2
 5 (LIMITED) Tier 1 Tickets: $30 (LIMITED) Tier 2 Tickets: $35 (LIMITED) Th
 is spring\, step into something softer\, sweeter\, and just a little bit s
 urreal. Whether you&#x27\;re welcoming the season in bloom or looking for 
 a night of beauty and escape\, Le Cabaret Bleu: Le Jardin des Papillons is
  your invitation into a dreamlike garden after dark. Consider this your wh
 imsical prelude to spring — or your main event. Step through the velvet 
 curtain into un jardin enchanté\, where fluttering butterflies\, blooming
  florals\, and cabaret magic intertwine. Think pastel decadence\, shimmeri
 ng wings\, delicate petals\, and just enough mischief to keep things inter
 esting. 🎶 La Musique Our live jazz ensemble will fill the room with air
 y swing\, romantic melodies\, and rhythms that feel like a warm spring bre
 eze. Expect lush brass\, dreamy vocals\, and a soundtrack made for dancing
  among the blossoms. 💃 Les Performeurs Dazzling burlesque and cabaret a
 rtists will drift through the evening like butterflies in bloom — sparkl
 ing\, sensual\, and impossible to look away from. Petals fall\, wings shim
 mer\, and the line between stage and audience disappears. 🍸 Les Showgir
 l Shots Our glamorous showgirls will flutter through the room with playful
  shots in hand\, inviting you to sip\, toast\, and indulge in true cabaret
  fashion. A little sweetness\, a little sparkle\, and a touch of spring ma
 gic. 🎭 Plus qu’un spectacle Interactive games\, загадки\, and 
 playful surprises await throughout the venue. Collect raffle tickets for y
 our chance to win enchanting prizes — because every garden holds a few s
 ecrets. 🦋 Tenue de Jardin Florals\, pastels\, soft silks\, sparkling wi
 ngs\, garden glamour — dress like you’ve just emerged from a butterfly
  dream. The more whimsical\, the better. 🗓 April 16th 📍 The Painted 
 Lady ⏰ Same time\, same place Welcome the season in style. Let the petal
 s fall\, the wings flutter\, and the magic bloom. Le Cabaret Bleu vous att
 end. 🦋✨ ‍
LOCATION:The Painted Lady\, 218 Ossington Avenue
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/le-cabaret-bleu-le-jardin-des-papillons
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
